      "padding": [
        44,
        48
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "kISPC",
          "name": "Title Block",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 10,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "FIuU4",
              "name": "Eyebrow",
              "fill": "$coral-hot",
              "content": "GROUPED ROWS",
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": 2.2
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "w6cYN6",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$text",
              "content": "A group header is a row that carries totals",
              "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
              "fontSize": 30,
              "fontWeight": "800",
              "letterSpacing": -0.7
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vYBTE",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$dim",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The header keeps the column grid, so each total sits under the column it totals. That is the whole reason to group: a collapsed group still answers what it cost and how many tokens it burned, and the reader never has to open it to compare two groups.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
